From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cellular: several modems: SIM slot, SIM icon, modems for mobile data and for calls
Description:
 The cellular library took the first modem for everything and named a SIM
 after the last part of its ModemManager object path, which changes with
 every start of ModemManager. With several modems (one per SIM, as on dual
 SIM phones whose modem has a modem object per SIM) mobile data, the quick
 setting and the status bar always followed the first modem.
 .
 CellularSim: slot (PrimarySimSlot of the modem when it reports SIM slots;
 read over D-Bus, ModemManagerQt has no API for it), name ("SIM <slot>",
 else the operator name of the SIM) and icon. The icon of a SIM is kept per
 ICCID in the shared file simidentitiesrc (class SimIdentities): a SIM seen
 for the first time gets the first icon of a fixed set that no known SIM
 has, and the choice is stored at once, so every application shows the same
 icon. The same file holds the SIM chosen for calls and text messages.
 .
 CellularModemList: dataModem, the modem whose NetworkManager device is
 connected or connecting, else the one with an autoconnect connection (one
 bound to its SIM first), else the one used last, else the first modem;
 setDataModem() enables mobile data on a modem. CellularModem: enabling
 mobile data with several modems disables it on the other modems, takes a
 connection of this modem even if none was used before and binds it to the
 SIM (gsm.sim-id). New connections are always bound to their SIM. There is
 no automatic fallback to another modem.
 .
 CellularModemList: defaultModem, the modem with the SIM chosen for calls
 and text messages (shared with the dialer and messaging applications),
 else the SIM in the first slot; setDefaultModem() chooses it.
 CellularModem: networkType, the radio access technology as named in the
 network-mobile-<strength>-<type> icons.
Forwarded: no
License: as the patched files (libs/cellular: LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL)
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
